  - "Position-stable WITHOUT re-anchoring" — the claim's sole distinctive mechanistic assertion — is empirically refuted by the claim's own L0: 85% of schema tokens are post-first-value, only 14.9% position-reusable (coincidental length alignment), RoPE tax 0.24–0.32 dominates, honest structural win over APC = 5–6% < 10% pre-registered threshold.
  - Prior-art pincer closes both forks of the claim's disjunction: WITHOUT re-anchor → weaker special case of Prompt Cache (Gim et al., MLSys 2024, arXiv:2311.04934); WITH re-anchor → collapses to CacheBlend (Yao et al., EuroSys 2025, arXiv:2405.16444). No novelty gap survives.
  - Same RoPE wall that killed EXP-0009 CDC-dedup (0.35–1.46% position-aware) fires here at 5–6% — more legible structure, identical physics.
